00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.320
So let’s get started, here’s my top 10
favorite anime characters.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.510
Number 10 - Guts from beserk.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:51.290
Easily one of the best swordsmen ever.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.750
The lone warrior archetype has always been
a favorite of mine.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.380
The story of his childhood is developed in
this incredible way and watching him become

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:00.920
a better fighter, largely without the aid
of magic is really cool.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:06.350
I feel like it’s hard for non-magical characters
to compete but his story is so compelling.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:07.530
Number 9 - Alucard from Hellsing.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:14.540
He’s Dracula, and all my favorite vampire
stories are dracula stories.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.350
But his fights are so much fun especially
with the addition of his taunts.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.080
Plus you wouldn’t expect to see Dracula
fight with guns.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:27.350
I’m also a big fan of the victorian outfit
and duster coat he wears.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.620
Number 8 - Spike Spiegel from Cowboy Bebop.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:34.400
He’s one of the best noir crime thriller
anime characters ever.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.950
He has this casual nature that really misleads
you into thinking he’s soft.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.180
But he’s one of the more violent characters
on my list.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:45.320
Favorite Spike episode hands down is ballad
of fallen angels.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.680
Number 7 - Levi from Attack On Titan.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.909
Yes he’s overpowered, but he’s the best
fighter on the best new anime series in the

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:52.909
world right now.

00:01:52.909 --> 00:01:54.830
He’s really the unsung hero of titan right
now.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.800
At least in the world of the show.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.590
The fandom gives him the credit he deserves.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.160
I’m interested to see if they de-power him
a little in season 2 though.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.080
Although it seems like everyone is secretly
a human form titan in disguise, so they may

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.280
not have to.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.129
Number 6 - Totoro from Totoro.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:14.260
He’s so ubiquitous around the world that
he became the avatar of studio ghibli.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.169
So you could argue that he’s so awesome
he has to be in every movie they make.

00:02:18.169 --> 00:02:19.319
At least in the logo.

00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:23.569
I’m sure if you looked hard enough you could
find him drawn in a background frame in all

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:24.739
their subsequent films.

00:02:24.739 --> 00:02:27.329
He’s like the R2D2 of anime.

00:02:27.329 --> 00:02:29.079
The best mascott ever.

00:02:29.079 --> 00:02:31.709
Number 5 - Kurapika from Hunter X Hunter 2011.

00:02:31.709 --> 00:02:32.950
The red eyes of vengeance.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.680
I love how
powerful the nen abilities made the character

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.099
and how they added all the restrictions to
keep it from getting ridiculous.

00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:40.959
Favorite fight though was watching him go
all out with Uvogin.

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:45.829
The phantom troupe arc is a good one to revisit
if you ever want to jump back into the series.

00:02:45.829 --> 00:02:48.129
Number 4 - Mikasa from Attack On Titan.

00:02:48.129 --> 00:02:52.689
Eren might be the real protagonist of the
series, but Mikasa is the most identifiable.

00:02:52.689 --> 00:02:54.329
Unless you count the titans.

00:02:54.329 --> 00:02:56.590
She’s the the backbone of the ensemble.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.819
She has to protect the person that has to
protect everyone.

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:06.279
For a long time I thought the show was secretly
about her.

00:03:06.279 --> 00:03:08.840
Number 3 - Lust from FMA Brotherhood.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:09.959
Favorite bad girl ever.

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:12.390
I definitely have a bias towards bad girls.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:16.342
She has the benefit of being a major character
for pretty much the entire series and it was

00:03:16.342 --> 00:03:20.130
so much fun watching her be downright evil,
then turn away from her mission and try so

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.279
badly to become human, just so she could die
permanently.

00:03:22.279 --> 00:03:29.189
My favorite lust scene was definitely her
last scene.

00:03:29.189 --> 00:03:32.459
Number 2 - Paprika from Paprika (2006) - She’s
like scarlett johansson’s character from

00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:36.370
her, living in the world of inception and
the matrix trilogy.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.609
She’s like the most epic digital avatar
in all of anime, so it’s only natural that

00:03:40.609 --> 00:03:43.470
the characters of them film manifest her to
lead them through the digital dream world.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:47.849
I guess you could argue that because dreams
and reality begin to merge, she is one of

00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:54.589
the most powerful anime characters of all
time.

00:03:54.589 --> 00:03:58.419
Number 1 - Edward Elric from FMA Brotherhood.

00:03:58.419 --> 00:04:01.609
I should really include alphonse on this list
two, because the brothers really need to be

00:04:01.609 --> 00:04:02.609
taken as a duo.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:05.659
If it weren’t for the two of them I don’t
think Brotherhood would have been one of the

00:04:05.659 --> 00:04:08.409
biggest anime shows on the planet.

00:04:08.409 --> 00:04:11.680
The reason Edward and said brother are my
favorite are because their characters can

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:16.540
swing so easily from funny to sad, and from
warriors to scientists and from normal kids

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.680
to tragic heroes.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.580
So as with all lists, there are a billion
awesome anime characters.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:24.220
Be sure to let me know who your favorites
are in the comments.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:29.870
I’m always looking for new characters to
knock some of these older ones off the list

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:37.710
and attack on titan has been the first in
a long time to do that.

